  values ('ME', 'short_answer', 'What are some challenges associated with the use of statistical learning in handling large-scale data sets? (5 marks)', 'Challenges include: (1) computation - huge volumes need large storage, memory and processing power, and algorithms must scale (distributed computing, parallel processing, stochastic or online methods); (2) data quality - big data are often noisy, incomplete, duplicated or inconsistent, and cleaning takes much effort; (3) variety and integration - combining structured and unstructured data from different sources and formats; (4) velocity - streaming data that must be analysed in real time; (5) high dimensionality - many variables relative to observations cause the curse of dimensionality and need feature selection or regularisation; (6) overfitting and spurious correlations - with so many variables some patterns appear by chance, so validation and multiple-testing control are needed; (7) interpretability - complex models such as deep learning are hard to explain to policymakers; (8) bias and representativeness - big data (e.g. social media) may not represent the population, and algorithms can reproduce bias; (9) privacy, confidentiality and security of personal data; and (10) shortage of skilled staff and infrastructure.', null, '[{"point": "Computational: storage, processing time, memory, need for distributed/ parallel computing, scalable algorithms", "marks": 1.5}, {"point": "Data issues: data quality, missing values, noise, heterogeneity/ integration of sources (variety), high dimensionality (curse of dimensionality), velocity/ streaming", "marks": 1.5}, {"point": "Statistical/ ethical: overfitting, spurious correlations and multiple testing, interpretability (''black box''), bias in data/ algorithms, privacy and confidentiality, skills shortage", "marks": 2}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge'),
    (select t.id from public.topics t where t.subject_id = (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge') and t.slug = 'statistics-general-subject-knowledge'), (select id from public.exam_papers where code = 'me-technical-2'), 'standard', 5,
